<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan increases oil product prices.</title>
<headline>Pakistan increases oil product prices.</headline>
<dateline>ISLAMABAD 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan has increased domestic oil product prices, newspapers reported on Thursday.</p>
<p>The reports said the move was in line with an existing policy of adjusting prices according to fluctuations in the exchange rate and oil prices abroad.</p>
<p>Oil product prices were last raised 10 percent on October 23, the day after ousted prime minister Benazir Bhutto's government devalued the rupee by 7.86 percent against the dollar as part of an economic stabilisation package.</p>
<p>Following are the new prices in rupees per litre:</p>
<p>				 Old price	 New Price    Increase</p>
<p>Motor gasoline (regular) 16.51	     16.81		0.30</p>
<p>Motor gasoline (super)   17.634	   17.922	     0.28</p>
<p>HOBC			   19.32	     19.59		0.27</p>
<p>SKO			     8.60		9.29		0.69</p>
<p>High speed diesel	   8.80		9.44		0.64</p>
<p>LDO			     7.01		7.62		0.64</p>
<p>JP-1			    7.60		8.06		0.46</p>
<p>JP-4			    9.44		9.90		0.46</p>
<p>Furnace oil/tonne     5,867.41	  6,116.37	    248.96</p>
</text>
